<section id="common-errors" class="py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
  <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-50">
    Common YAML Errors and How to Fix Them
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Even experienced developers run into these YAML pitfalls. Here is how to spot and fix the most frequent syntax errors.</p>
  <div class="mt-10 space-y-4">
    {[
      { num: '1', title: 'Tabs instead of spaces', desc: 'YAML does not allow tab characters for indentation. Use spaces only. Most editors can be configured to insert spaces when you press Tab. Our formatter immediately flags tab characters and shows the exact line where they appear.', code: '# Bad (tab character ->)\nkey:\n->\tsubkey: value\n\n# Good (spaces)\nkey:\n  subkey: value' },
      { num: '2', title: 'Missing colon after key', desc: 'Every YAML mapping key must be followed by a colon and a space before the value. Forgetting the colon or the space after it produces a parsing error.', code: '# Bad\nname John\n\n# Good\nname: John' },
      { num: '3', title: 'Inconsistent indentation', desc: 'All items at the same nesting level must have identical indentation. Mixing 2-space and 4-space indents within the same block breaks the YAML structure.', code: '# Bad\nparent:\n  child1: a\n    child2: b  # 4 spaces instead of 2\n\n# Good\nparent:\n  child1: a\n  child2: b' },
      { num: '4', title: 'Confusing strings with booleans', desc: 'In YAML 1.1, unquoted values like yes, no, on, off, true, false are interpreted as booleans. YAML 1.2 fixed this, but many tools still use 1.1. Always quote ambiguous values.', code: '# Dangerous (YAML 1.1)\ncountries:\n  - yes  # becomes boolean true\n  - no   # becomes boolean false\n\n# Safe\ncountries:\n  - "yes"\n  - "no"' },
      { num: '5', title: 'Nested mappings without indentation', desc: 'When a value is itself a mapping, it must be indented under its key. Forgetting to indent produces a parser error.', code: '# Bad\nperson:\nname: John\nage: 30  # not indented under person\n\n# Good\nperson:\n  name: John\n  age: 30' },
      { num: '6', title: 'Duplicate keys', desc: 'YAML does not allow duplicate keys within the same mapping. The second occurrence silently overwrites the first, which can cause hard-to-find bugs.', code: '# Bad (second "port" overwrites first)\nserver:\n  port: 8080\n  host: localhost\n  port: 9090\n\n# Good\nserver:\n  host: localhost\n  port: 9090' },
    ].map(({num, title, desc, code}) => (
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80 bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-red-100 dark:bg-red-900/30 text-red-600 dark:text-red-400 text-xs font-bold mr-2">{num}</span>
          {title}
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">{desc}</p>
        <pre class="mt-3 p-4 rounded-lg bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-950 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-700 text-xs font-mono text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed">{code}</pre>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>
